A ball detector trained on bright daylight footage may fail at night or in shadows.
Solution: Train/test the ball detector on a variety of lighting conditions from the start, not just one type of footage.

Camera not centered behind the goal
If the camera is placed slightly to one side rather than dead-center behind the goal, the whole geometry skews, and left/right accuracy suffers.
Solution: Either enforce a fixed setup position (mark it physically) or calculate the camera's off-center angle during calibration and correct for it mathematically.

Different balls, different sizes
A futsal ball, a size-4 ball, and a size-5 ball are all different real diameters — if your system assumes one fixed ball size for depth calculations, using the wrong ball breaks the math.
Solution: Let the user select/enter the ball type/size before starting, or auto-calibrate using a known reference frame at the start.
